{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are implementing GitHub issue #12 in user/delegate (`gh issue view 12`, and the rulings in `gh issue view 12 --comments`; spec #4). Do not delegate further: no subagents, no cursor_run, no delegate tools. Follow AGENTS.md. Stay on branch `12-budgets` in this worktree; do not create branches.\n\nGoal: performance budgets as tests against fake agents.\n- A wall-clock budget for every command: `run` (until the process exits; it exits right after printing the job id), `resume`, `cancel` (on a RUNNING job whose fake agent exits on SIGTERM), `watch` (on an already-terminal job, no timeout path), `doctor` (fakes exit 0), `models`.\n- A resident-memory budget for the supervisor while a fake agent holds RUNNING: read `supervisorPid` from the job's status record and sample `ps -o rss= -p <pid>` (KB). Same command on macOS and Linux; no cfg.\n\nFile fence: owns a new `tests/budgets.rs`. You may copy the small helpers you need from `tests/cli_e2e.rs` (the fake agent script, the release-file pattern, `until`). Do not edit `tests/cli_e2e.rs` unless extracting a shared helper is clearly smaller. Forbidden: `src/` (no production changes), `.github/`, everything else. If a budget cannot be met without a production change, stop and report.\n\nMethod:\n1. Write the tests with placeholder budgets. Measure each command 5 times locally; take the median.\n2. Set each budget to about 3x the median, rounded up, as a constant with a comment beside it in exactly this form:\n   `const RUN_BUDGET_MS: u128 = 60; // measured: 18ms on M-series Mac, budget 3x`\n   Memory likewise: `const SUPERVISOR_RSS_BUDGET_KB: u64 = 12000; // measured: 3900KB on M-series Mac, budget 3x`\n3. Fake agents wait on release files, never sleeps, for RUNNING-state measurements (lesson from #7). Every spawned process is reaped (release or kill + wait). The whole file must finish under 60s. No retries on timing failures.\n4. Measure the release of the `delegate` binary the tests already use (`env!(\"CARGO_BIN_EXE_delegate\")`); budgets apply to the debug test build CI also uses.\n\nGates before committing: `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test` all pass. Run `cargo test --test budgets` 3 times; all green.\n\nNegative control (acceptance criterion 3): after green, temporarily add `std::thread::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_millis(500));` in `src/cli.rs` right before `run` prints the job id, run `cargo test --test budgets`, copy the failing assertion message verbatim, then REVERT the sleep (git checkout src/cli.rs) and confirm green. Do not commit the sleep.\n\nCommit only tests/budgets.rs (and an extracted helper if you made one) with a conventional message ending `Co-Authored-By: Composer 2.5 <noreply@cursor.com>`. Do not push.\n\nCompletion bar: report the commit SHA, a compact table of command → median → budget, the negative-control failing assertion text verbatim, and the 3-run results — or a failure triage; nothing in between. Then **Friction**: up to 3 bullets on what slowed you, what this brief got wrong or left out, what you'd change (\"none\" is fine). End with a STATUS line.\n\nEnd your final message with a single trailing line that is exactly one of: STATUS: DONE, STATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS, STATUS: BLOCKED, STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT, or STATUS: ERROR. When you need an answer from the orchestrator before you can proceed, put your question in the message body and end with STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT."}]},"session_id":"23269ead-5209-4ac9-9976-6eab6d468682"}
