{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"tool_97b61c3d-9d5e-45cf-b66c-68a6d03c77d","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/Users/user/work/delegate-12-budgets/tests/cli_e2e.rs","limit":200},"result":{"success":{"content":"//! Drives the real `delegate` binary as a process against a fake cursor-agent.\n\nuse serde_json::Value;\nuse std::io::Write;\nuse std::os::unix::fs::PermissionsExt;\nuse std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\nuse std::process::{Command, Output, Stdio};\nuse std::time::{Duration, Instant};\n\nconst FAKE_AGENT: &str = r#\"#!/bin/sh\nprintf '%s\\n' \"$@\" > \"$(dirname \"$0\")/argv.txt\"\nrel=\"$(dirname \"$0\")/go\"\n# Stays RUNNING behind a grandchild: `sleep` inherits the agent's process group, so\n# killing only the agent would leave it behind.\ncase \"$*\" in\n  *CANCELME*)\n    sleep 300 &\n    echo $! > \"$(dirname \"$0\")/grandchild.pid\"\n    echo $$ > \"$(dirname \"$0\")/agent.pid\"\n    i=0\n    while [ ! -e \"$rel\" ] && [ \"$i\" -lt 400 ]; do sleep 0.05; i=$((i+1)); done\n    printf '%s\\n' '{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"result\":\"late\\nSTATUS: DONE\",\"session_id\":\"s-9\"}'\n    exit 0\n    ;;\nesac\n# Silent jobs emit nothing, so the model-idle window is what kills them.\ncase \"$*\" in\n  *SILENT*)\n    i=0\n    while [ ! -e \"$rel\" ] && [ \"$i\" -lt 400 ]; do sleep 0.05; i=$((i+1)); done\n    exit 0\n    ;;\nesac\nprintf '%s\\n' '{\"type\":\"tool_call\",\"subtype\":\"started\",\"tool_call\":{\"shellToolCall\":{\"args\":{\"command\":\"ls\"}}}}'\ncase \"$*\" in\n  *SLOW*)\n    i=0\n    while [ ! -e \"$rel\" ] && [ \"$i\" -lt 400 ]; do sleep 0.05; i=$((i+1)); done\n    ;;\nesac\ncase \"$*\" in\n  *COMMIT*)\n    printf 'x\\n' >> calc.py\n    git add calc.py && git commit -q -m \"Fix add\"\n    ;;\nesac\ncase \"$*\" in\n  *DIRTY*)\n    printf 'x\\n' >> calc.py\n    git add calc.py && git commit -q -m \"Fix add\"\n    printf 'leftover\\n' >> extra.py\n    ;;\nesac\ncase \"$*\" in\n  *ASKME*) printf '%s\\n' '{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"result\":\"Which db?\\nSTATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT\",\"session_id\":\"s-2\"}' ;;\n  *) printf '%s\\n' '{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"result\":\"391\\nSTATUS: DONE\",\"session_id\":\"s-1\"}' ;;\nesac\n\"#;\n\nstruct Env {\n    dir: PathBuf,\n}\n\nimpl Env {\n    fn new(name: &str) -> Self {\n        let dir = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(\"cdm-cli-{name}-{}\", std::process::id()));\n        let _ = std::fs::remove_dir_all(&dir);\n        std::fs::create_dir_all(&dir).unwrap();\n        let agent = dir.join(\"agent.sh\");\n        std::fs::write(&agent, FAKE_AGENT).unwrap();\n        std::fs::set_permissions(&agent, std::fs::Permissions::from_mode(0o755)).unwrap();\n        Env { dir }\n    }\n\n    /// Waits for the CANCELME fake to write its pids; on timeout, shows the job record.\n    fn until_agent_spawned(&self, id: &str) {\n        let t = Instant::now();\n        while !(self.dir.join(\"agent.pid\").exists() && self.dir.join(\"grandchild.pid\").exists()) {\n            assert!(\n                t.elapsed() < Duration::from_secs(10),\n                \"timed out: agent spawn; record: {}\",\n                self.record(id)\n            );\n            std::thread::sleep(Duration::from_millis(20));\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// Lets SLOW jobs finish; until then they stay RUNNING (10s cap).\n    fn release(&self) {\n        std::fs::write(self.dir.join(\"go\"), \"\").unwrap();\n    }\n\n    fn argv(&self) -> Vec<String> {\n        let s = std::fs::read_to_string(self.dir.join(\"argv.txt\")).unwrap();\n        s.lines().map(String::from).collect()\n    }\n\n    fn delegate(&self, args: &[&str], stdin: Option<&str>) -> Output {\n        self.delegate_env(args, stdin, &[])\n    }\n\n    fn delegate_env(&self, args: &[&str], stdin: Option<&str>, env: &[(&str, &str)]) -> Output {\n        let mut cmd = Command::new(env!(\"CARGO_BIN_EXE_delegate\"));\n        cmd.args(args)\n            .current_dir(&self.dir)\n            .env(\"TMPDIR\", &self.dir)\n            .env(\"CURSOR_AGENT_BIN\", self.dir.join(\"agent.sh\"))\n            .env(\"DELEGATE_HEARTBEAT_MS\", \"100\");\n        for (k, v) in env {\n            cmd.env(k, v);\n        }\n        let mut child = cmd\n            .stdin(Stdio::piped())\n            .stdout(Stdio::piped())\n            .stderr(Stdio::piped())\n            .spawn()\n            .unwrap();\n        let mut si = child.stdin.take().unwrap();\n        if let Some(s) = stdin {\n            let _ = si.write_all(s.as_bytes());\n        }\n        drop(si);\n        child.wait_with_output().unwrap()\n    }\n\n    /// Starts a job and returns its id.\n    fn run(&self, prompt: &str) -> String {\n        self.ok(&[\"run\", \"--model\", \"composer-2.5\"], prompt, &[])\n    }\n\n    fn ok(&self, args: &[&str], prompt: &str, env: &[(&str, &str)]) -> String {\n        self.ok_output(&self.delegate_env(args, Some(prompt), env))\n    }\n\n    fn ok_output(&self, out: &Output) -> String {\n        assert!(\n            out.status.success(),\n            \"exit {:?}\\nstderr: {}\\nstdout: {}\",\n            out.status.code(),\n            String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stderr),\n            String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stdout)\n        );\n        String::from_utf8(out.stdout.clone())\n            .unwrap()\n            .trim()\n            .to_string()\n    }\n\n    fn run_write(&self, prompt: &str) -> Output {\n        self.delegate(\n            &[\n                \"run\",\n                \"--model\",\n                \"composer-2.5\",\n                \"--capability\",\n                \"read-write\",\n            ],\n            Some(prompt),\n        )\n    }\n\n    fn record(&self, id: &str) -> Value {\n        let p: PathBuf = self.dir.join(\"delegate-jobs\").join(format!(\"{id}.json\"));\n        serde_json::from_str(&std::fs::read_to_string(p).unwrap()).unwrap()\n    }\n\n    fn wait_terminal(&self, id: &str) -> Value {\n        let out = self.delegate(&[\"watch\", id, \"--timeout\", \"10\"], None);\n        assert_eq!(out.status.code(), Some(0));\n        serde_json::from_slice(&out.stdout).unwrap()\n    }\n}\n\nimpl Drop for Env {\n    fn drop(&mut self) {\n        let _ = std::fs::remove_dir_all(&self.dir);\n    }\n}\n\nfn alive(pid: i64) -> bool {\n    unsafe { libc::kill(pid as i32, 0) == 0 }\n}\n\nfn until(what: &str, mut f: impl FnMut() -> bool) {\n    let t = Instant::now();\n    while !f() {\n        assert!(t.elapsed() < Duration::from_secs(10), \"timed out: {what}\");\n        std::thread::sleep(Duration::from_millis(20));\n    }\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn run_returns_id_while_job_runs_then_it_finishes() {\n    let e = Env::new(\"run\");\n    let id = e.run(\"SLOW do it\");\n    assert_eq!(id.len(), 36);\n    let r = e.record(&id);\n    assert_eq!(r[\"status\"], \"RUNNING\");\n    assert_eq!(r[\"resume\"][\"model\"], \"composer-2.5\");\n    assert_eq!(r[\"resume\"][\"capability\"], \"read-only\");","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":912,"fileSize":29190,"path":"/Users/user/work/delegate-12-budgets/tests/cli_e2e.rs","readRange":{"startLine":1,"endLine":200},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"tool_97b61c3d-9d5e-45cf-b66c-68a6d03c77d","startedAtMs":"1790851637619","completedAtMs":"1790851638296"},"model_call_id":"03ff5b5c-012a-4c9e-8b5f-f8530a892bb5-0-zr3p","session_id":"23269ead-5209-4ac9-9976-6eab6d468682","timestamp_ms":1790851638213}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"tool_8b5229fa-60ad-490a-b947-adbfb90b232","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/Users/user/work/delegate-12-budgets/docs/agents/issue-tracker.md"},"result":{"success":{"content":"# Issue tracker: GitHub\n\nIssues and specs live in GitHub Issues on this repo. Use `gh`; it infers the repo from the clone.\n\n- **Publish** (a spec, a ticket): `gh issue create`, multi-line body from a heredoc or `--body-file`.\n- **Fetch a ticket**: `gh issue view <n> --comments`.\n- **Labels**: the triage vocabulary is in `triage-labels.md`.\n- **Triage covers issues only.** Pull requests here are the owner's own work and never enter the triage queue.\n\n## Wayfinding\n\n`/wayfinder` keeps a **map**: one issue labelled `wayfinder:map` holding Notes, Decisions so far, and Fog. Its tickets are child issues.\n\n- **Child ticket**: a GitHub sub-issue of the map, labelled `wayfinder:<research|prototype|grilling|task>`. Without sub-issues, list the child in a task list in the map body and open the child body with `Part of #<map>`.\n- **Blocking**: native issue dependencies. Add an edge with `gh api --method POST repos/<owner>/<repo>/issues/<child>/dependencies/blocked_by -F issue_id=<blocker-db-id>`. The blocker's database id comes from `gh api repos/<owner>/<repo>/issues/<n> --jq .id`; the `#number` and `node_id` are rejected. Without dependencies, open the child body with `Blocked by: #<n>, #<n>`. A ticket is unblocked once every blocker is closed.\n- **Frontier**: the map's open children with zero open blockers (`issue_dependencies_summary.blocked_by`) and no assignee; the first in map order wins.\n- **Claim**: `gh issue edit <n> --add-assignee @me`, as the session's first write.\n- **Resolve**: comment the answer, close the issue, then append a one-line pointer (gist + link) to the map's Decisions so far.\n","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":19,"fileSize":1618,"path":"/Users/user/work/delegate-12-budgets/docs/agents/issue-tracker.md","readRange":{"startLine":1,"endLine":19},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"tool_8b5229fa-60ad-490a-b947-adbfb90b232","startedAtMs":"1790851637604","completedAtMs":"1790851638298"},"model_call_id":"03ff5b5c-012a-4c9e-8b5f-f8530a892bb5-0-zr3p","session_id":"23269ead-5209-4ac9-9976-6eab6d468682","timestamp_ms":1790851638227}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"tool_0b5657a5-02c1-47b4-809d-84d756693e7","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-12-budgets && gh issue view 12 && gh issue view 12 --comments","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"tool_0b5657a5-02c1-47b4-809d-84d756693e7","simpleCommands":["cd","gh","gh"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":false,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"cd","args":[{"type":"word","value":"/Users/user/work/delegate-12-budgets"}],"fullText":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-12-budgets"},{"name":"gh","args":[{"type":"word","value":"issue"},{"type":"word","value":"view"},{"type":"number","value":"12"}],"fullText":"gh issue view 12"},{"name":"gh","args":[{"type":"word","value":"issue"},{"type":"word","value":"view"},{"type":"number","value":"12"},{"type":"word","value":"--comments"}],"fullText":"gh issue view 12 --comments"}],"hasRedirects":false,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"redirects":[]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"View GitHub issue #12 and comments","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"23269ead-5209-4ac9-9976-6eab6d468682","adminCommandDenylist":[],"requestId":"03ff5b5c-012a-4c9e-8b5f-f8530a892bb5"},"result":{"success":{"command":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-12-budgets && gh issue view 12 && gh issue view 12 --comments","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"title:\tLatency and supervisor-memory budgets\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tuser (Amogh Akshintala)\nlabels:\tready-for-agent\ncomments:\t1\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\tuser/delegate#11, user/delegate#10, user/delegate#9\nblocking:\tuser/delegate#13\nnumber:\t12\n--\n## Parent\n\n#4\n\n## What to build\n\nPerformance budgets as tests, measured against fake agents:\n\n- # a wall-clock budget for every command: `run` returning its job id, `resume`, `cancel`, `watch` on a finished job, `doctor`, `models`\n- # a resident-memory budget for the supervisor while a fake agent runs\n\nBudgets are about 3x the local measurement so CI noise does not trip them. Record the measured values in the test so the margin is visible.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- # [ ] Each command has a timing test with a stated budget.\n- # [ ] The supervisor memory test passes locally and on Linux CI.\n- # [ ] Making `run` artificially slow (e.g. a sleep before printing the id) fails the test.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- #9 Gate, change-set, watchdog and cross-process write lock\n- #10 resume (with overrides) and cancel\n- #11 models and trimmed doctor, with the new model table\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings: orchestrator ruling (owner asleep; reversible)\n\n1. **Slow-run negative control:** no test-only delay hook in production code. The lane records the negative control in the PR instead: it adds a local sleep before `run` prints its id, shows the test failing, then removes the sleep.\n2. **Supervisor memory:** sample `ps -o rss= -p <supervisorPid>` (the pid comes from the status record) while the fake agent holds RUNNING. The same command works on macOS and Linux, so the test needs no per-OS code.\n3. **Latency endpoint:** wall clock until the process exits. `run` and `resume` exit right after printing the id.\n4. **Cases timed:** `watch` on an already-terminal job, with no timeout path. `cancel` on a RUNNING job whose fake agent exits on SIGTERM. `doctor` against fakes that exit 0.\n5. **Budget constants:** about 3x the local measurement, with the measured baseline in a comment beside each. No retries: if CI is noisy, raise the margin.\n6. **Fake agents** wait on release files, never on sleeps (the lesson from #7).\n--\n","stderr":"","executionTime":2767,"interleavedOutput":"title:\tLatency and supervisor-memory budgets\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tuser (Amogh Akshintala)\nlabels:\tready-for-agent\ncomments:\t1\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\tuser/delegate#11, user/delegate#10, user/delegate#9\nblocking:\tuser/delegate#13\nnumber:\t12\n--\n## Parent\n\n#4\n\n## What to build\n\nPerformance budgets as tests, measured against fake agents:\n\n- # a wall-clock budget for every command: `run` returning its job id, `resume`, `cancel`, `watch` on a finished job, `doctor`, `models`\n- # a resident-memory budget for the supervisor while a fake agent runs\n\nBudgets are about 3x the local measurement so CI noise does not trip them. Record the measured values in the test so the margin is visible.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- # [ ] Each command has a timing test with a stated budget.\n- # [ ] The supervisor memory test passes locally and on Linux CI.\n- # [ ] Making `run` artificially slow (e.g. a sleep before printing the id) fails the test.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- #9 Gate, change-set, watchdog and cross-process write lock\n- #10 resume (with overrides) and cancel\n- #11 models and trimmed doctor, with the new model table\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings: orchestrator ruling (owner asleep; reversible)\n\n1. **Slow-run negative control:** no test-only delay hook in production code. The lane records the negative control in the PR instead: it adds a local sleep before `run` prints its id, shows the test failing, then removes the sleep.\n2. **Supervisor memory:** sample `ps -o rss= -p <supervisorPid>` (the pid comes from the status record) while the fake agent holds RUNNING. The same command works on macOS and Linux, so the test needs no per-OS code.\n3. **Latency endpoint:** wall clock until the process exits. `run` and `resume` exit right after printing the id.\n4. **Cases timed:** `watch` on an already-terminal job, with no timeout path. `cancel` on a RUNNING job whose fake agent exits on SIGTERM. `doctor` against fakes that exit 0.\n5. **Budget constants:** about 3x the local measurement, with the measured baseline in a comment beside each. No retries: if CI is noisy, raise the margin.\n6. **Fake agents** wait on release files, never on sleeps (the lesson from #7).\n--\n","localExecutionTimeMs":2243},"isBackground":false},"description":"View GitHub issue #12 and comments"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"tool_0b5657a5-02c1-47b4-809d-84d756693e7","startedAtMs":"1790851637616","completedAtMs":"1790851640575"},"model_call_id":"03ff5b5c-012a-4c9e-8b5f-f8530a892bb5-0-zr3p","session_id":"23269ead-5209-4ac9-9976-6eab6d468682","timestamp_ms":1790851640503}
