{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Commit\n\n`f15e200c0397c26b39f3ecf9383916b2a3da8561`\n\n## Budgets (median → budget)\n\n| Command | Median | Budget |\n|---------|--------|--------|\n| `run` | 34ms | 102ms |\n| `resume` | 31ms | 93ms |\n| `cancel` | 64ms | 192ms |\n| `watch` | 2ms | 6ms |\n| `doctor` | 189ms | 567ms |\n| `models` | 2ms | 6ms |\n| supervisor RSS | 2912KB | 8736KB |\n\nMedians: 5 serial samples per command on M-series Mac (with pre-timed `watch nope` warmup).\n\n## Negative control (verbatim)\n\n```\nrun took 545ms, budget 102ms\n```\n\n(from `assert!` at `tests/budgets.rs:214` after temporary 500ms sleep before `run` prints the job id; sleep reverted)\n\n## `cargo test --test budgets` (3 runs)\n\n| Run | Result |\n|-----|--------|\n| 1 | 7 passed, ~1.91s |\n| 2 | 7 passed, ~1.84s |\n| 3 | 7 passed, ~1.92s |\n\nGates: `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, and full `cargo test` all passed.\n\n## Friction\n\n- Parallel integration tests caused large cold-start spikes until a throwaway `watch` warmup and a file-level mutex serialized budget tests.\n- Brief did not say whether timing should include process cold load; medians without warmup were misleading (e.g. `run` max 267ms vs median 34ms).\n- `doctor` still spiked above 3× median under full-suite CPU load once; warmup plus serial mutex stabilized local runs but Linux CI may need a margin bump if it flakes.\n\nSTATUS: DONE"}]},"session_id":"23269ead-5209-4ac9-9976-6eab6d468682"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":374862,"duration_api_ms":374862,"is_error":false,"result":"Implementing performance-budget tests for issue #12. Gathering the issue spec and existing test patterns.\n\n\nCreating `tests/budgets.rs` and calibrating budgets.\n\n\nUpdating budgets from medians and removing the calibration test.\n\n\nSerializing budget tests and re-measuring with `--test-threads=1` to reduce parallel noise.\n\n\nAdding a warmup delegate invocation before each timed sample to stabilize cold-start outliers.\n\n\n## Commit\n\n`f15e200c0397c26b39f3ecf9383916b2a3da8561`\n\n## Budgets (median → budget)\n\n| Command | Median | Budget |\n|---------|--------|--------|\n| `run` | 34ms | 102ms |\n| `resume` | 31ms | 93ms |\n| `cancel` | 64ms | 192ms |\n| `watch` | 2ms | 6ms |\n| `doctor` | 189ms | 567ms |\n| `models` | 2ms | 6ms |\n| supervisor RSS | 2912KB | 8736KB |\n\nMedians: 5 serial samples per command on M-series Mac (with pre-timed `watch nope` warmup).\n\n## Negative control (verbatim)\n\n```\nrun took 545ms, budget 102ms\n```\n\n(from `assert!` at `tests/budgets.rs:214` after temporary 500ms sleep before `run` prints the job id; sleep reverted)\n\n## `cargo test --test budgets` (3 runs)\n\n| Run | Result |\n|-----|--------|\n| 1 | 7 passed, ~1.91s |\n| 2 | 7 passed, ~1.84s |\n| 3 | 7 passed, ~1.92s |\n\nGates: `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, and full `cargo test` all passed.\n\n## Friction\n\n- Parallel integration tests caused large cold-start spikes until a throwaway `watch` warmup and a file-level mutex serialized budget tests.\n- Brief did not say whether timing should include process cold load; medians without warmup were misleading (e.g. `run` max 267ms vs median 34ms).\n- `doctor` still spiked above 3× median under full-suite CPU load once; warmup plus serial mutex stabilized local runs but Linux CI may need a margin bump if it flakes.\n\nSTATUS: DONE","session_id":"23269ead-5209-4ac9-9976-6eab6d468682","request_id":"03ff5b5c-012a-4c9e-8b5f-f8530a892bb5","usage":{"inputTokens":52697,"outputTokens":20621,"cacheReadTokens":1533254,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
